+- [ ] 1.1 Add the documented whole-token, case-insensitive rule for allowlisted Russian repeated flanged shorthand (including supported dot/space variations), applying it before generic joining-abbreviation expansion; verify the canonical alternate contains one flanged term and preserves product, DN, PN, and all unrelated source tokens.
+- [ ] 1.2 Preserve strict boundaries and catalog-domain anchoring for the rule; add focused unit tests proving mixed-side pairs, embedded lookalikes, unknown codes, and unsupported product text do not gain or collapse a connection meaning.
