+- Emit one catalog-native connection term in the optional canonical retrieval query while retaining every unrelated source term.
+- Preserve original-query retrieval, one-alternate-query limits, per-modality deduplication/RRF, original reranker input, and result text.
+- Add focused tests for supported shorthand, punctuation/case variants, unsafe lookalikes, and fail-open retrieval behavior.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `symmetric-connection-canonicalization`: Creates a bounded additive retrieval representation for unambiguous repeated end-connection shorthand.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- None.
+
+## Impact
+
+- Affected package code: `src/nomenclature_matcher/query_canonicalization.py`, with focused wiring changes only if needed to retain the existing hybrid retrieval contract.
+- Affected tests: query-canonicalization and hybrid-retriever/matcher mock regressions.
+- No DeepSeek prompt, catalog content, embedding model, Qdrant payload, BM25 corpus, collection alias, or full index rebuild is required.
