+## 1. Symmetric connection canonicalization
+
+- [ ] 1.1 Add the documented whole-token, case-insensitive rule for allowlisted Russian repeated flanged shorthand (including supported dot/space variations), applying it before generic joining-abbreviation expansion; verify the canonical alternate contains one flanged term and preserves product, DN, PN, and all unrelated source tokens.
+- [ ] 1.2 Preserve strict boundaries and catalog-domain anchoring for the rule; add focused unit tests proving mixed-side pairs, embedded lookalikes, unknown codes, and unsupported product text do not gain or collapse a connection meaning.
+
+## 2. Retrieval contract regression coverage
+
+- [ ] 2.1 Add or update mocked hybrid-retriever tests to verify a clean symmetric-shorthand alternate is queried in addition to the original, candidates are deduplicated by LD id, and original candidates survive an alternate-query error.
+- [ ] 2.2 Add or update matcher integration coverage showing the source tender text, rather than the canonical alternate, remains the reranker input and `MatchResult.query` for a supported shorthand query.
+
+## 3. Verification
+
+- [ ] 3.1 Run focused canonicalization, hybrid-retriever, and matcher tests, then run `python -m pytest -q`; resolve failures without expanding the allowlist to ambiguous `FF` or mixed connection forms.

